{"content":[{"c":["RAGUEL"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["1. KJV spelling of Reuel, an alternate name for Jethro, Moses’ father-in-law, in ",{"href":"?bref=Num.10.29","r":"Num.10.29","rawR":"Num.10.29","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Num.10.29","value":"Num.10.29"}],"t":"ref","v":"Numbers 10:29"},". ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Jethro_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Jethro_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Jethro_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Jethro"},"."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"},{"c":["2. A member of the tribe of Naphtali living in Ecbatana who, according to ",{"href":"?bref=Tb.3.7","r":"Tb.3.7","rawR":"Tb.3.7","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Tb.3.7","value":"Tb.3.7"}],"t":"ref","v":"Tobit 3:7"},", was the father of Sarah, soon to become the wife of Tobias, thanks to the intervention of the angel Raphael."],"sourceClass":"list","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Raguel","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Numbers 10:29","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Num.10.29","rawQueryValue":"Num.10.29","sourceRefExact":"Num.10.29"},{"anchorText":"Tobit 3:7","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Tb.3.7","rawQueryValue":"Tb.3.7","sourceRefExact":"Tb.3.7"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"e028df2e851842065399cd2fd3bd2875b02d369cd4b9e61997f03b2c7f96d900","sourceItemName":"Raguel","sourceItemOrder":20,"sourceMember":"Articles/R.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Raguel","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Raguel","title":"Raguel","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}